---

# 1. Project Overview

HR360 is an integrated Human Resource Management and Analytics System designed to centralize employee information and key HR processes within a structured digital platform.

The system will support employee lifecycle management, workforce status monitoring, attendance, leave management, performance management, Performance Improvement Plans (PIPs), employee training, recruitment and management analytics.

The solution is being developed as an end-to-end web application consisting of:

* React/Vite frontend
* Node.js and Express.js backend
* PostgreSQL relational database
* REST APIs
* Analytics services
* Management dashboards
* Planned Microsoft Power BI integration
* Git/GitHub based version control

The project follows an Agile/Scrum delivery approach, allowing functionality to be developed, tested and reviewed incrementally.

---

# 2. Business Need / Problem Statement

HR activities are often managed through multiple spreadsheets, disconnected records and manually prepared reports. This can create difficulties in maintaining consistent employee information, monitoring workforce activity, tracking employee lifecycle events and producing timely management reports.

The absence of a centralized HR information structure can also result in:

* Duplicate or inconsistent employee information
* Manual status tracking
* Limited visibility into workforce availability
* Difficulty monitoring attendance and leave
* Limited performance and PIP visibility
* Fragmented training records
* Manual recruitment pipeline tracking
* Time-consuming management reporting
* Inconsistent KPI definitions

HR360 is intended to address these challenges by establishing a centralized HR data model, standardized business rules, REST APIs and analytics capabilities.

---

# 3. Project Purpose

The purpose of HR360 is to provide a structured HR management platform that enables authorized users to manage core HR processes consistently while providing reliable operational and management information.

The system will establish a common data foundation that can support both transactional HR operations and future Business Intelligence requirements.

---

# 4. Business Objectives

The primary objectives of HR360 are to:

1. Centralize employee and HR operational data in PostgreSQL.
2. Standardize employee lifecycle and workforce status management.
3. Implement department-specific employee active-status business rules.
4. Digitize attendance and leave management.
5. Support performance reviews and Performance Improvement Plans.
6. Centralize employee training information.
7. Digitize recruitment activities from candidate registration through job offers.
8. Provide REST APIs for controlled access to HR data.
9. Provide management-level analytics and KPI reporting.
10. Establish a foundation for Microsoft Power BI integration.
11. Improve data consistency, traceability and reporting capability.
12. Demonstrate an end-to-end Agile/Scrum software delivery lifecycle.

---

# 5. Project Scope

## 5.1 In Scope

The HR360 project includes:

### Employee Management

* Employee master data
* Employee identification
* Department assignment
* Job role assignment
* Employment lifecycle
* Work status
* Salary status
* Department-specific active-status determination

### Workforce Management

* Department management
* Job role management
* Work-status management
* Employee availability monitoring

### Attendance

* Attendance records
* Attendance status
* Check-in/check-out information
* Working hours
* Attendance reporting

### Leave Management

* Leave types
* Leave balances
* Leave requests
* Leave approval workflow
* Leave reporting

### Performance Management

* Performance reviews
* Performance ratings
* Performance feedback
* Performance Improvement Plans

### Training Management

* Training programs
* Employee training enrollment
* Training attendance
* Completion tracking
* Training scores
* Certification tracking

### Recruitment

* Candidate management
* Job applications
* Interview management
* Interview feedback
* Job offers
* Recruitment status tracking

### Analytics

* HR overview KPIs
* Department analytics
* Attendance analytics
* Leave analytics
* Performance analytics
* Training analytics
* Recruitment analytics

### Technical Scope

* PostgreSQL database
* Node.js/Express backend
* REST API layer
* React/Vite frontend
* Git/GitHub source control
* Power BI integration planning

---

# 6. Out of Scope

The following items are outside the initial project scope:

* Full payroll processing
* Statutory payroll calculations
* Biometric attendance device integration
* Native Android/iOS applications
* Advanced AI-based recruitment decisions
* Automated external job-board integrations
* Enterprise-wide ERP integration
* Complex compensation and benefits administration
* Advanced identity-management integration

These capabilities may be considered in future releases through formal scope change procedures.

---

# 7. Key Business Rules

| Rule ID | Business Rule                                                                                           | Expected Result                     |
| ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| BR-001  | HR employees are active when `employment_status = EMPLOYED`.                                            | Active status = ACTIVE              |
| BR-002  | Operations employees are active when work status is `WORKING` or `ONLINE`.                              | Active status = ACTIVE              |
| BR-003  | Finance employees are active when `salary_status = PAID`.                                               | Active status = ACTIVE              |
| BR-004  | Active status is determined using department-specific rules rather than one universal rule.             | Correct departmental classification |
| BR-005  | Employee lifecycle includes Candidate, Probation, Employed, On Leave, Resigned, Terminated and Retired. | Standardized lifecycle              |
| BR-006  | Recruitment records use controlled candidate/application statuses.                                      | Traceable recruitment pipeline      |
| BR-007  | HR360 should derive departmental active status rather than store a single global active flag.           | Reduced status inconsistency        |

