# 9. Stakeholder Governance

The project will use the following governance model:

**Product Owner → Business Requirements → Product Backlog → Sprint Planning → Development → Testing → Sprint Review → Acceptance → Release**

Business stakeholders will participate in requirement clarification, review and acceptance.

Technical implementation decisions will be documented by the Developer/Technical Lead.

Requirements will be maintained by the Business Analyst and linked to functional requirements, user stories, test scenarios and final traceability documentation.

---

# 10. Agile / Scrum Delivery Approach

HR360 will follow an Agile/Scrum methodology.

### Product Backlog

The backlog will contain:

* Epics
* User stories
* Acceptance criteria
* Technical tasks
* Defects
* Documentation activities

### Sprint Planning

Selected backlog items will be refined and planned for implementation.

### Development

Development will include:

* Database development
* Backend development
* API development
* Frontend development
* Integration
* Testing

### Sprint Review

Completed functionality will be demonstrated to stakeholders.

### Sprint Retrospective

The team will identify:

* What worked
* What did not work
* Process improvements
* Actions for the next sprint

### Definition of Done

A backlog item is considered complete when:

* Requirement is understood
* Development is completed
* Business logic is implemented
* Testing is completed
* Acceptance criteria are satisfied
* Documentation is updated where applicable
* Code is committed to Git
* Changes are pushed to GitHub
* No unresolved critical defect remains

---

# 11. Technology Landscape

| Layer           | Technology           | Purpose                                 |
| --------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| Frontend        | React + Vite         | HR user interface                       |
| Backend         | Node.js + Express.js | REST APIs and business logic            |
| Database        | PostgreSQL 18        | Transactional HR data                   |
| API             | REST / JSON          | Frontend-backend communication          |
| Analytics       | HR360 Analytics APIs | KPI and reporting data                  |
| BI              | Microsoft Power BI   | Management dashboards                   |
| Version Control | Git / GitHub         | Source control and project traceability |

Python is not part of the application implementation stack.

